WEBVTT

00:46:57.121 --> 00:47:00.329
and we're talking to each other
and crying and embracing for

00:47:00.329 --> 00:47:02.996
the last time. And it's very
emotional in the book.

00:47:02.996 --> 00:47:04.704
I'm crying, you know, I'm like, it's sad.

00:47:04.746 --> 00:47:09.163
And then, you know, I'm standing there
with Reese Witherspoon right before she's

00:47:09.163 --> 00:47:12.121
going to walk into the street with Thomas
Sadowski, who plays my ex-husband.

00:47:12.413 --> 00:47:14.163
And they're going to begin
shooting the scene.

00:47:14.163 --> 00:47:18.246
And she suddenly looks at me and
she just just starts sobbing.

00:47:19.704 --> 00:47:22.704
She was getting ready for that scene
and they go into the street

00:47:22.704 --> 00:47:24.829
and they shoot this, and I'm standing
next to the director,

00:47:24.829 --> 00:47:26.704
I'm watching this on the camera.

00:47:26.871 --> 00:47:29.996
And I noticed that some people on the
crew were kind of gathered around me

00:47:29.996 --> 00:47:33.663
and a couple of them sort of put their
hand on my back and put their hand